xnu 0275: bucket the frame and event intervals finely, and count event gaps

The coarse `20-33`/`over33` buckets cannot tell a drag that alternates 16 and 33
ms from one whose frames drift between 17 and 25 ms, and the two want different
fixes. The frame gap is now printed with a minimum and in six buckets, and the
touch path reports the interval between the events it hands to the HID side in
the same buckets: a drag moves when an event lands, so events delivered in
bursts step the content however healthy the per-second count looks.

Both lines are printed once a second with the fps line.

